{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 310,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's cut to the chase: as of July 4, 2012,\nthe Higgs Boson is the last fundamental piece"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5230,
    "dDurationMs": 3439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the Standard Model of Particle Physics\nto be discovered experimentally. \"But,\" you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8669,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "might ask, \"why was the Higgs Boson included\nin the Standard Model alongside well-known"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12629,
    "dDurationMs": 3631,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particles like electrons and photons and quarks\nif it hadn't been discovered back then in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16260,
    "dDurationMs": 3350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the 1970s?\" Good question. There are two main\nreasons:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19610,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, just like the electron is an excitation\nin the electron field, the Higgs boson is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23990,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simply a particle which is an excitation of\nthe everywhere-permeating Higgs field. The"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28190,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Higgs field, in turn, plays an integral role\nin our model for radioactive decay, called"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31010,
    "dDurationMs": 4279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the weak nuclear force (in particular, the\nHiggs field helps explain why it's so weak)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35289,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We'll talk more about this in a later video,\nbut even though weak nuclear theory was confirmed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38929,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the 1980s, in the equations the Higgs field\nis so inextricably jumbled with the weak force"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43569,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that until now we've been unable to confirm\nits actual and independent existence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47359,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second reason to include the Higgs in\nthe standard model is some jargony business"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50499,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about the Higgs field giving all other particles\nmass. But why does stuff need to be \"given\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54389,
    "dDurationMs": 3981,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mass in the first place? Isn't mass just an\nintrinsic property of matter, like electric"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58370,
    "dDurationMs": 5449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "charge? Well, in particle physics…no. Remember\nthat in the Standard Model, we first write"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63819,
    "dDurationMs": 3221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down a mathematical \"ingredients list\" of\nall the particles that we think are in nature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67040,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(and their properties). You can watch my \"theory\nof everything\" video for a quick refresher."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71040,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We then run this list through a big fancy\nmathematical machine, which spits out equations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74720,
    "dDurationMs": 1870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that tell us how these particles behave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76590,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Except, if we try to include mass as a property\nfor the particles on our ingredients list,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80860,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the math-machine breaks. Maybe mass was a\npoor choice… but most particles we observe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85740,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in nature do have mass, so we have to figure\nout some clever way of using ingredients that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90020,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will spit out mass in the final equations\nwithout it being an input - kind of like how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93810,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can let yeast, sugar and water ferment\ninto alcohol that wasn't there to begin with."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98020,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as you may be thirstily anticipating,\nthe solution is to toss a yeasty Higgs field"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102080,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in with the other ingredients of the Standard\nModel, so that when we let the math ferment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105350,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we get out particles that have mass! But this\nmodel also brews up something we DIDN'T intend:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110070,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a solitary Higgs particle, the infamous boson.\nAnd since the model works so well to explain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115210,
    "dDurationMs": 4449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everything else, we figured it was pretty\nlikely that the lonely boson is right, too!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119659,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To summarize, the Higgs Boson is a particle\nwhich is a left-over excitation of the Higgs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123659,
    "dDurationMs": 4581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "field, which in turn was needed in the Standard\nModel to 1) explain the weak nuclear force"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128240,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 2) explain why any of the other particles\nhave mass at all. However, the boson is the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132530,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only bit of the Higgs field which is independently\nverifiable, precisely because the other bits"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136550,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are tangled up in the weak nuclear force and\nin giving particles mass. The fact that the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140360,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Higgs Boson is so independent from the rest\nof the Standard Model is why it's the last"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143910,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "piece of the puzzle to be discovered - and\nif it turns out to be exactly what was predicted,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147750,
    "dDurationMs": 1730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Standard model will be complete."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149480,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only problem is that we know that the\nstandard model ISN'T a complete description"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152760,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the universe (it entirely misses out on\ngravity, for example). So to physicists, it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157080,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be much more interesting AND helpful\nif the Higgs boson turns out to be not quite"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160530,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what we expect… then we might get a clue\nas to how to reach a deeper understanding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163860,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the universe. So even though we just made\na discovery, we can't sit back and relax."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167930,
    "dDurationMs": 920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We need a hint, Mr. Higgs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168850,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Continued in Parts II and III"
    } ]
  } ]
}
